--TEST--
A class that gets one method from two interface defaults, or from a default and a delegate, does not compile, and the error names every source — `rule:classes/member-conflict-is-an-error`
--FILE--
<?nvs
interface Greets {
    public function hello(): string { return "hi"; }
}

interface Welcomes {
    public function hello(): string { return "welcome"; }
}

interface Speaks {
    public function hello(): string;
}

class Host implements Greets, Welcomes {}

class Voice implements Speaks {
    public function hello(): string { return "voice"; }
}

class Desk implements Greets, Speaks by $voice {
    private Speaks $voice;
    public function constructor(Speaks $voice) { $this->voice = $voice; }
}
echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/interfaces
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0859]: `Host` gets `hello` from more than one source: the default in `Greets`, the default in `Welcomes`
%A
error[E0859]: `Desk` gets `hello` from more than one source: the default in `Greets`, `Speaks` through `$voice`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
